on is unambiguous.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'its cache-credited PASS count strictly exceeds the attempt before it (the first FAIL's credited count is the baseline)' — no mention of how the count is measured.","close_autoresume.py:54-63 _cache_credited_count counts `r.get('met') is True and r.get('seeded') is True`; completion_verdict_assembly.py:176-186 stamps `seeded: true` for cache-seeded PASSes.","Risk: an executor could instead count overall met:true records; a fresh (non-cached) PASS would then inflate the count and defeat the anti-spin guarantee the plan promises."],"finding":"The plan's progress/counter decision rule ('cache-credited PASS count strictly exceeds the attempt before it', Mechanism section 4) never defines HOW the cache-credited count is derived from the verdict. The framework computes it from the per-criterion `seeded: true` marker (records that are met:true AND seeded:true), but the plan text names neither `seeded` nor the derivation, so the counter's placement/definition is ambiguous.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1126c9af93657592","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanism section 4 ('Bounded by count AND by progress') / AC 'Progress condition'","norm_id":"n73e9f27ce19eb7ad","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Second attempt banks a fresh PASS but zero NEW cache-seeded credit; a naive 'count met:true' progress measure would read this as progress and dispatch an identical-remainder spin the plan's progress bound is meant to stop."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In Mechanism section 4, replace 'cache-credited PASS count' with an explicit definition: 'the count of per-criterion records the assembly seam stamped `seeded: true` (met:true, credited from the cross-run verdict cache)', naming the marker and where it is set.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"